# GeoSeq stage S8: the finite certificate data of `thm:K4` (generated by script, checked in Lean)

Source coordinate `0` of a carry, depth `j = 8` (the other sources follow by the rotation symmetry
`K4_rot`). `K4A`: reached state vectors after a nonzero digit, `K4B`: before it (first entry = the
initial vector `initV4`), states stored as triples of natural numbers (`decV`); `K4tA`, `K4tB`: the
transition tables (digit `r` sends state `s` to entry `r` of row `s`; `K4tB` entries `1, 2, 3` point into
`K4A`); `K4out`: readout index (state ↦ tuple); `K4tup`: the `37` readout tuples (`48` codes of
`D_i(l)[c][0]` at `3i + c` and `D_i(l-1)[c][0]` at `24 + 3i + c`, codes `0, 1, 2, 3` for `0, 1, ω, ω²`);
`K4wit`: per tuple the base-4 digits (least significant first) of the first carry length with that
tuple; `K4Z`: the `67` change columns of `eq:carrychange` as binary words (one word per target
coordinate, digit `i` in bits `2(7-i), 2(7-i)+1`); `K4chg`: per tuple the indices in `K4Z` of
`ω² D(l)` (`Δ(y) = ω²`) and `D(l) + ω D(l-1)` (`Δ(y) = 1`). The data were produced by a breadth-first
search outside Lean; nothing here is trusted: every property used is checked by kernel `decide` in
`GeoSeq/K4Cert.lean`.
-/

